{"title":"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><ol><li>This is a fifteen question free-response test. Each question has exactly one integer answer.</li>\n<li>You have 60 minutes to complete the test.</li>\n<li>You will receive 4 points for each correct answer, and 0 points for each problem left unanswered or incorrect.</li>\n<li>Figures are not necessarily drawn to scale.</li>\n<li>No aids are permitted other than scratch paper, graph paper, rulers, and erasers. No calculators, smartwatches, or computing devices are allowed. No problems on the test will require the use of a calculator.</li></ol>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the sum of all positive multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> that are factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/f/3afdbc1109a0d51befd8c26e6fbabc35f82e82c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$27.$\" width=\"21\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three distinct even positive integers are chosen between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/a/36af3a317653fc5ff424093b4df40c2b4d5a6f5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"31\" height=\"16\" /> inclusive. What is the largest possible average of these three integers?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a regular octagon, the sum of any three consecutive sides is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/f/03fa3795d07527af8700c3fded230607baf1fec4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90.$\" width=\"21\" height=\"12\" /> A square is constructed using one of the sides of this octagon. What is the area of the square?\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Octagonsquare.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/bf/Octagonsquare.jpg/250px-Octagonsquare.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"250\" height=\"254\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/bf/Octagonsquare.jpg/375px-Octagonsquare.jpg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/b/bf/Octagonsquare.jpg/500px-Octagonsquare.jpg 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</center>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/9/069e14d8586e65674ce72115fbc3d3672d0bf3af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{x+2}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"44\" height=\"37\" /> is its own reciprocal, find the product of all possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/3/fc3be04db73828946870d3ccc6d122395a4bacf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/9/969339e9f440bbcb8d0aac2c628ac5e6d7ceb4fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n!=n \\cdot (n-1) \\cdot (n-2) \\cdots 2 \\cdot 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"251\" height=\"20\" /> for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. Find the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> that satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/d/36df42c0f356e92ee3bcdca3abaa75bc4387fd5b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{5!x}{2022!}=\\frac{20}{2021!}.\\]\" width=\"116\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />, diagonal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> bisects both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/5/cb55dc9c50a80e1d9eb23fe53e45f464c0ac755e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"59\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/3/23386faeefe37629243fa264877b288499db5048.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BCD$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/1/841477a87e41ca9c72a3c11eaabb6cf25ccd4977.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/f/50fde934b870fb9c1fc6a9092cc49004288c218e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=13$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, find the perimeter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> each represent a single digit and they satisfy the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/2/d92d1fb62e2b18f640a996cd6d7f7f0ed2cf655b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{array}{cccc}&amp; A &amp; B &amp; C \\\\ \\times &amp; &amp;  &amp;3 \\\\ \\hline  &amp; 7 &amp; 9 &amp; C\\end{array},\\]\" width=\"127\" height=\"53\" /> find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/c/9ac7d2411693670b46d540962b74d7b97697a90c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3A+2B+C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"105\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems/Problem 7\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many triangles are bounded by segments in the figure and contain the red triangle? (Do not include the red triangle in your total.)\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Sprint2_.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/f2/Sprint2_.png/300px-Sprint2_.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"300\" height=\"293\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/f2/Sprint2_.png/450px-Sprint2_.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/f/f2/Sprint2_.png/600px-Sprint2_.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</center>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems/Problem 8\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/e/68e922271b873159ed842b7a2fef678e2bda3f53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1,x_2,\\ldots,x_{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"107\" height=\"11\" /> is a strictly increasing sequence of positive integers that satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/1/ad108b31c7b45c0ccab98e7ff977b0ef95f8c89f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2}&lt;\\frac{2}{x_1}&lt;\\frac{3}{x_2}&lt; \\cdots &lt; \\frac{11}{x_{10}},\\]\" width=\"205\" height=\"39\" /> find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/0/e9088b4ee603fe3d37f39ae1a5f660d440e81927.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1+x_2+\\cdots+x_{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"150\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems/Problem 9\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a certain school, each class has an equal number of students. If the number of classes was to increase by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then each class would have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> students. If the number of classes was to decrease by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then each class would have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> students. How many students are in each class?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems/Problem 10\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/7/ee730ecd30681b47e111b69adcc41031307559c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a : b : c : d=1 : 2 : 3 : 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"188\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/e/65e844b013cb07a4ccd130fcea1b7ab985ba0b3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$252$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, what is the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems/Problem 11\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A rectangle with base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is inscribed in an equilateral triangle. Another rectangle with height <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is also inscribed in the triangle. The base of the second rectangle can be written as a fully simplified fraction <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/e/40ef7c2ccddab492a260f3d0a444a9d907816219.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{a+b\\sqrt{3}}{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"70\" height=\"43\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/7/b977623001c7231965610580b12895977c8cefdf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$gcd(a,b,c)=1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"122\" height=\"20\" /> Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/b/6ebd1e0356cfe09c0d9b5459d6f1542657bb5891.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a+b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Sprint13.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/7/77/Sprint13.jpg/400px-Sprint13.jpg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"318\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/7/77/Sprint13.jpg/600px-Sprint13.jpg 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/7/77/Sprint13.jpg 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</center>\n<p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems/Problem 12\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be nonnegative integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/a/8aa41005dc1d3365767006b3d0bd30f0b26ea1ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+y)^2+(xy)^2=25.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"177\" height=\"21\" /> Find the sum of all possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/3/fc3be04db73828946870d3ccc6d122395a4bacf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"10\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems/Problem 13\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the leftmost digit of the product <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/c/7cca56c840db1d2457346e67fff42c3701c000fc.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\underbrace{161616 \\cdots 16}_{100 \\text{ digits }} \\times \\underbrace{252525 \\cdots 25}_{100 \\text{ digits }}?\\]\" width=\"228\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems/Problem 14\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/4/c54e7152acd659788861f0453ac195c635e0a005.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> define the function <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/f/eef0203e65664bd00b5f0325c5c5fcd81bcead8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> to output <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/b/99b3ffa03230545edbc57a7bd273925580081174.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\underbrace{777 \\cdots 7}_{n\\ \\text{sevens}}5.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"95\" height=\"38\" /> For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/5/785bb02130c9fb3215906c972a6807832f424604.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1)=475$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"87\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/3/a43841ba641efed9962ff90c70710df36c58b495.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2)=4775$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/3/67379e0d09ca455bcda754d46eb41dd7c4895d31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(3)=47775.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"18\" /> Find the last three digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/4/244944bb29f9d9d942d159a2b7178e3b06f5728a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{f(1)+f(2)+ \\cdots + f(100)}{25}.\\]\" width=\"214\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Problems/Problem 15\">Solution</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ol><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Sprint_Problems\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Sprint Problems\">2021 Sprint Accuracy Problems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Invitationals_Problems\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Invitationals Problems\">2021 JMPSC Invitationals Problems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_JMPSC_Accuracy_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 JMPSC Accuracy Answer Key\">2021 JMPSC Accuracy Answer Key</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=JMPSC_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"JMPSC Problems and Solutions\">All JMPSC Problems and Solutions</a></li></ol>\n<p>The problems on this page are copyrighted by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://jmpsc.org\">Junior Mathematicians' Problem Solving Competition</a>. <span class=\"mw-valign-middle\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:JMPSC.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ab/JMPSC.png/120px-JMPSC.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"120\" height=\"120\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/a/ab/JMPSC.png/180px-JMPSC.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/a/ab/JMPSC.png 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017131232\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.052 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.100 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 344/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 183/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9927/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    8.534      1 Template:JMPSC_Notice\n100.00%    8.534      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:21597:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017131232 and revision id 158138. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}